WEBVTT

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:04.230
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:14.040
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.150
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.170
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.850
<i>Hey, were you listening?</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.450
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:04.170
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:12.190
Kiyomitsu!

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:12.930
It went that way!

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.110
Got it!

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.220
Amazing!

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:24.120
35 - Tantou 
<b>Hakata Toushirou</b>

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:21.750
I'm popular!

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.110
This is how I do business!

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.660
Yes, well, I'm taking your customers.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.570
Hey! No cutting in line!

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.100
<i>Okita-kun's strength wasn't 
only with his sword.</i>

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:39.590
<i>He had a strength that made 
those around him feel warm inside.</i>

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:42.620
<i>Can I really be like Okita-kun?</i>

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.240
When the weather is this nice, 
it makes me want to take a nap.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.850
You can't. We have to go 
on expedition after this.

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.390
Right...

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.020
Our mission is to investigate Edo this time.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.160
Who is the expedition captain again?

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.740
Mutsunokami, I believe.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.920
Man, Mutsunokami.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.120
He gets pretty fired up, 
even about expeditions.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.330
An expedition?

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:14.670
Leave it to me!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.670
It doesn't become a field trip just 
because you're motivated, right?

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.880
Expeditions and field trips are 
totally different things.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:20.880
Something bad has happened!

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.200
Something bad has happened!

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.860
Something bad has happened!

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.360
What's the matter?

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.600
Master has a fever!

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.050
What?

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.050
Eh?

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:32.550
They're overworked from 
having to assign dispatches,

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.550
expeditions, duties, smithing, and
 creating armor day and night.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.480
They never leave their 
room, and with the lack of

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.560
sufficient exercise, it's only 
natural their health would suffer.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.900
I'm not fit to be Master's attendant,
since I couldn't prevent this.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.090
What should I do?

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.820
First, shouldn't we just 
do the best that we can?

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.380
That's true.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.040
First, we need medicine.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.130
You'll want the fruit from
the Asiatic dogwood then.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.520
Asiatic dogwood?

00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.380
What's that?

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:00.880
This.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.620
It relieves fevers, supplements nutrition,
and reduces fatigue.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.810
Okay, please make a medicine with that.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.840
I'll give it to Master.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.230
I'm sorry.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.080
I'm all out of it right now.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.450
Is that so? Then I'll go to the general store.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.310
The store doesn't sell it.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.840
What should we do, then?!

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.680
We'll need to gather more.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:19.820
I'll go gather it!

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.830
But where?

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.740
This tree was brought 
from outside the country

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.800
and used in pharmacology in the Edo period.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:26.570
After that...

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.170
We're going on expedition 
to the Edo period in a bit.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.860
Where would it be in Edo?

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.940
That much I don't know.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.990
You might be able to find one or 
two of the trees in the woods.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.660
What's the matter, Hasebe?

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.820
Investigating Edo is your mission.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.490
Master's orders are absolute.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.460
You can't neglect them.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.840
However,

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.970
it would be different if you just happened
to find that tree, and brought some back.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:53.890
Hasebe!

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:58.840
Understood.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.030
Master has a fever?!

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.770
It's my fault.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.810
It's not your fault, Hasebe-kun.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:08.410
No, one of my jobs is to 
look after Master's health.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.140
Come now, don't get so down about it.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:13.440
They'll recover fast if 
they eat something good.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.240
"Eat" is written with characters
 for "people" and "recover," after all.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.690
What should we have them eat, then?

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:22.000
They won't have much of an 
appetite due to the fever.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.540
Something they can easily eat that 
will be nutritious would be best.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.290
That's it (<i>hata</i>)!

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.880
Shokudaikiri, I've got it.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.720
<b>Grouper</b>

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:31.100
Grouper (<i>hata</i>)?

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.530
What about udon?

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:33.900
Udon, huh?

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.340
With udon,

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.740
even if they don't have an appetite,
they can suck in the noodles and broth.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:41.620
And udon is quickly absorbed 
into the system, too.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.030
Udon it is.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:50.190
Then leave it to me.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.080
Wait.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.690
I want to make Master better.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.690
I'll make the udon.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.630
Please watch over me from 
there, Shokudaikiri.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:00.900
Okay.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:05.120
Make the brine.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:09.280
Pour it into the flour.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:13.260
Stir it by hand.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.060
So you're going to make the noodles first.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:21.390
Knead the dough.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.570
You really know what you're 
doing, Hasebe-kun.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.510
No, only somewhat.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:44.080
If I make a mistake, please tell me.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:47.950
Will do.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:07:00.390
And now, we have to let it rest.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.600
Let it rest?!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.530
That's right. For an hour.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:07.960
We can't do that!

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:13.680
This can't wait an hour.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.240
Yeah, I thought it'd come to that.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:21.610
Why?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:31.500
Because I was thinking of 
making it for today's dinner.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.920
I will gladly use it.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:47.660
Place the plastic over the 
dough and tread on it.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.990
To be stepping on something 
Master will eat...

00:07:54.000 --> 00:08:05.630
Stepping on the dough allows
you to make perfectly firm udon noodles.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.750
Do your best.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:13.630
Okay, next, I have to let it rest again.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:14.880
Let it rest?!

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:16.500
It can't be!

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.010
Sprinkle on the flour.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:26.010
Stretch it out with a rod.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:30.020
Fold it.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.440
And cut.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:42.020
Look, Shokudaikiri.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:46.030
The noodles are done.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:49.140
Now, what should I use for the ingredients?

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.890
Something delicious and good
 for the body would be best.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.240
Fried tofu.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.130
Nakigitsune!

00:08:55.270 --> 00:09:02.310
Because there isn't anybody 
who hates kitsune udon.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.130
That's right.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:05.200
Fried tofu?

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.270
That's a good idea.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.290
There should be some in the refrigerator—

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:11.250
Mikazuki?!

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:16.140
Wouldn't eggs be a great ingredient for udon?

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.180
Tsukimi Udon.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:24.020
It's nutritious, so it will 
quickly heal any illness.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:27.420
I see. If that's the case, then 
please allow me to make it.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.160
Thank you.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:35.370
<i>Master, when we return from battle 
bruised and beaten, you gently comfort us,</i>

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:38.280
<i>and reward us with a smile when 
we return from our activities.</i>

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:42.460
<i>When I think about it, we have constantly 
been in receipt of your favor.</i>

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.650
<i>Now it's my turn!</i>

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:46.980
<i>I will save you, Master!</i>

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.860
<i>No matter what!</i>

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:51.900
<i>Master!</i>

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.440
<i>Don't die!</i>

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.760
Are they really that sick?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.810
I'm pretty sure it's just a cold.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.980
The nabeyaki udon is finished!

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:10.470
It's a bit awkward with so many ingredients,
 but the biggest issue is the taste.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.930
Shall I have my tongue play with it then?

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:16.710
I mean to taste it.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.710
Nikkari Aoe!

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.210
Why can't you show up normally 
like everyone else?

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:22.660
Oh, I see.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:26.900
Aoe-kun belonged to the Kyougoku family of 
the Marugame Domain in the Sanuki Province,

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.890
so he's very familiar with udon.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.740
I-Is that so? Then please try some.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.740
Thank you.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:38.690
This is?!

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.610
The noodles are short and thin,

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.830
with a deep flavor that goes 
smoothly down the throat.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:48.300
It's like the "banshuu udon" eaten 
in the hometown of Kuroda Kanbei.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:54.130
Hasebe-kun, did you consciously 
make it like this, or not?

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.430
You must have recalled that you
served the Kuroda family in the past.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.620
Does that mean it was good?

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:06.000
That's all that matters, then.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.480
It's the first time I've ever made 
udon since coming to this citadel.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.990
I'll make Master feel better with this!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.980
<b>Stingy!</b>

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.980
<b>You can't have any.</b>

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.700
Huh, so this is Edo?

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.950
37 - Yari
 <b>Otegine</b>

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.960
I bet it's crawling with 
Japanese business men.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:27.320
We have a lot of first-timers 
on this expedition, don't we?

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:31.160
Our mission for this expedition 
is to investigate Edo.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.260
We'll collect our observations

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:35.810
on the climate and the way
the people live in the survey form.

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:37.270
We have two hours.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.710
Ka, ka, ka!

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:41.820
Fighting and expeditions are training.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:44.470
36 - Tachi
 <b>Yamabushi Kunihiro</b>

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:44.730
Now then, where should we start, Captain?

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.020
Let's see...

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:46.960
Wait a minute!

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.840
What is it, Kashuu?

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.270
The truth is, Master has a fever.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.420
The Master does?

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:53.660
Fever?

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:54.580
Is it a cold?

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.220
We don't know.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.720
When we talked to Yagen,

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:00.820
he told us of a red fruit from the
Asiatic dogwood that can relieve fevers.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:03.750
Yagen said that it is here somewhere in Edo.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:06.610
There should be one or two 
trees if we go in the forest.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.350
So, do we have to do the investigation?

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:15.300
The Edo investigation is over.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.330
I'll write up the investigation report.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:21.330
The most important thing right 
now is healing Master's illness.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:24.900
We will definitely return
with the Asiatic dogwood.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.850
Whoops, it's not this way.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.360
It's this way!

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:31.990
Ka, ka, ka!

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:35.100
Traversing forests and 
mountains is my specialty.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:40.060
Yamabushi Kunihiro, our goal is to find the 
Asiatic dogwood. There's no need to hurry.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.970
Ka, ka, ka!

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:43.620
So it is, so it is.

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:46.140
He really likes mountains, doesn't he?

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:49.760
By the way, Kashuu, why 
does Master have a fever?

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.760
Red fruit, red fruit.

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:51.860
Now that you mention it,

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:55.110
the light in Master's room
has been on late at night lately.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:56.530
Late at night?

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.000
I wonder what they're doing?

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.340
Isn't it obvious?

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:01.840
Checking the stock market!

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.800
<b>Stock Market?</b>

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:03.220
Stock?

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.290
Market?

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:08.940
They want to tackle the next day of trading, 
so they check all the stocks late at night.

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:13.120
It could be that Master 
dabbles in trading at night.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.940
If not stocks, there's also the foreign
 exchange market, though.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:17.060
Hakata, you'll get left behind.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.390
I was just joking.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.750
Otegine!

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.140
Are you sure you're looking?

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:27.860
I am, but I'm not very good with 
anything other than stabbing things.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:29.470
That looks heavy.

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:31.020
It's not that bad.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.480
Probably just a little over 20 kilograms.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.190
When it comes to stabbing 
things, I can't lose!

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:39.820
Huh?

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:42.670
What is it?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.530
A race?

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:44.840
They're really into it.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:58.930
You said you had no talent other than 
stabbing things, but that made things worse!

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.550
Really sorry about that.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:03.320
We got...

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:05.560
...separated from everyone.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.420
That's totally fine.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.950
It's wiser to split up and search.

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.320
We'll go on ahead.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.920
Which means, Yamabushi, 
are we climbing this?

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.840
You're right.

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:20.670
What are you trying to do, Yamabushi?

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.200
Roar, my muscles!

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:24.970
Fight!

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:29.210
Hakata Toushirou, you're supposed
to say "ippatsu!" in return!

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.940
Why would you do that?

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:35.040
Ka, ka, ka!

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.760
Can you pull me up with some 
vines that are up there?

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:40.240
Vines?

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.900
Will this work?

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.440
Hold on tight!

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.350
Leave it to me.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:47.980
Here I go!

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.810
Leave it to... You're heavy!

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:57.300
Guess there's no choice.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:15:00.430
Roar, my muscles!

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:01.790
Fight!

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:01.790
Again?!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.890
Ippatsu!

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:07.580
Don't these look like Asiatic dogwood fruit?

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.610
Only the color is the same.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:11.820
They look delicious.

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.100
Should I try some?

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.090
Jeez, if anything happens, 
it's your own fault.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.760
This is no good.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.050
I can't win against my curiosity.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:21.590
If they taste good, I'll give
 them to Shokudaikiri.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:29.540
Ah, it's so cold and refreshing!

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:32.610
K-Kashuu!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.300
Otegine!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.350
I'm saved.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.950
I'm sorry, Otegine.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.040
Kashuu!

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.380
We can't seem to find any Asiatic dogwood.

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:43.060
Ouch!

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:43.750
What happened?

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.330
A trap?

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:47.940
It's okay.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:49.550
I'll figure it out myself.

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:50.460
Hakata!

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.770
Don't push yourself.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.090
Why don't we carefully make our way back?

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:57.660
I won't go back!

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:59.530
I can walk on my own feet.

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:01.660
We've come all this way. 
We can't turn back now.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.530
I want to heal Master's illness.

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:07.300
It's only been a few days 
since I came to the citadel.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.620
But I want to be useful,

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.240
and quickly become a part of the citadel, too.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.050
I feel the same way you do.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:20.620
Okay, Hakata Toushirou, 
you will ride on my back!

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.580
I feel bad having you carry me like this.

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.240
Ka, ka, ka!

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:30.820
I, too, want to exist for our Master.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:34.040
I want to be strong enough 
to laugh everything away,

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:36.690
to smile no matter what the situation is.

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:39.500
What's the matter, Hakata Toushirou? Smile!

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:43.630
If you smile, the next path will open up.

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:46.680
Ka, ka, ka!

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.150
Now, let's go!

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.570
Ka, ka, ka!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:54.020
We've walked quite a bit, but we 
have to be back in two hours.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.240
Jeez, Asiatic dogwood! Where are you?!

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.140
Mutsunokami, don't just stop suddenly—

00:16:59.140 --> 00:16:59.480
Shh!

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:08.420
Yamatonokami, don't draw your sword.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.890
Keep it in its sheath.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:12.850
Yamatonokami!

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.020
Better to finish it before it finishes us.

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:16.300
Compose yourself.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.790
Can't you do something with your gun?

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.370
Even if I hit it with the few 
bullets I have, it won't die.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:26.590
Besides, we just want to pass
 through. There's no need to kill it.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:32.020
Won't you please put your 
sword in its sheath?

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:35.520
Please, will you let us pass?

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.620
Our master has been beset by an illness.

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:44.040
Our master gave us these bodies, and it's 
because of our master that we're here now.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:46.480
We can't do anything without our master,

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:48.730
so we wish to make them better.

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:51.670
We love our master.

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:55.780
We simply wish to take back 
some medicine for our master.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:57.430
Please.

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:00.300
Will you let us pass through 
without baring your fangs?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:02.280
We're both living creatures.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.950
We can communicate with our hearts.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.370
It's all right.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:32.010
Sakamoto Ryouma guided 
the Satsuma and Choushuu,

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:34.790
who got along like cats and 
dogs, to a reconciliation.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:39.480
If we speak with our hearts, 
we don't need swords or guns.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:43.210
To think that Ryouma's spirit would 
be useful in a place like this.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.070
There's no time.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.370
Let's move on.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:46.950
Right.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.860
We should reach the cliff any minute now.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:54.800
Yeah.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.060
We seem to have made it in time.

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.230
Hey!

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.540
You two are late!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:05.920
We did it!

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:07.650
We have to hurry back with it.

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:08.250
Ow!

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:09.910
Are you all right?

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:12.460
I'm finally doing something for Master.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.380
I'm not worried about a little wound.

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:17.660
Besides, a special rare fruit 
may be worth some money!

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:28.890
Yagen!

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.760
We brought back the Asiatic dogwood fruit!

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.020
And lots of it.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.180
Well?

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.510
This should last us for a while.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.550
Can you make it quickly?

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:40.560
Leave it to me.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:41.820
We did it.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:42.480
Yeah.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.740
I've finished the purification.

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:49.190
Thank you, Ishikirimaru.

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:53.020
I want to do anything
 I can for Master, as well.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.670
Hasebe-san, you made udon?

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:58.400
Yes, I made it for Master.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:03.590
As Master's attendant, I, Hasebe, 
made udon for the first time.

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:05.550
Is it good?

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.130
Eh? It's a little salty?

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:08.630
I wonder why?

00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:13.440
Um...

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:23.160
Summer Vacation Beach Day Trip!
 (Requested) 
Let's make some memories!

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:18.150
I wrote a letter, but is it 
okay for me to take it up?

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:20.500
Yeah, I think it should be.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:27.520
Everyone, Master ate the udon!

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.560
Good for you.

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:31.880
I gave the medicine Yagen made to Master.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:33.000
They were pleased.

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:34.490
Good.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.380
We are swords.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:42.100
It is our pleasure to be used by Master.

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:44.690
It's not good if they don't stay healthy.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.560
I'm sure everyone else feels the same.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.070
Everyone...

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:04.200
For our master...

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.210
That's right.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.430
Yasusada?

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:10.140
Eh?

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.440
What's wrong?!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.930
It's our master!

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:16.890
I want to be stronger for Master, too!

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:19.080
I want to go tell them that!

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:22.050
Yamatonokami. Master is eating right now.

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:23.120
You can tell them later—

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:25.100
It has to be right now!

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:26.090
Hey!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.700
Listen, Yamatonokami!

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:30.350
Master has a fever!

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.990
Talk to them after they've gotten better!

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:31.690
Jeez.

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:35.270
Hey, listen when I'm talking to you!

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:39.880
Swimsuits and...

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.080
...a loincloth.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:45.630
Oh, I wanted to go to the ocean
next month with everyone,

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.200
so I sent in a request to Master for these.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.480
Why not just buy swimsuits?

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:51.230
Am I right?

00:21:51.230 --> 00:21:52.740
There's not enough money.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:54.700
Do you know why that is?

00:21:55.070 --> 00:21:58.550
Because in April, everyone spent it 
needlessly at the general store!

00:21:58.550 --> 00:22:02.050
Then I guess I troubled them by saying
that I wanted to go to the ocean

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.680
even though we're broke.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:05.300
They're handmade.

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:08.830
They said it was their first 
time sewing anything.

00:22:08.830 --> 00:22:10.610
Everyone cares for Master.

00:22:10.610 --> 00:22:12.580
And Master cares for everyone.

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:14.600
This citadel is truly blessed.

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:17.320
We have to give thanks to Master.

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:18.440
That's right.

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:20.020
That's true, but...

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:21.490
What about this?

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:24.640
Who's going to wear it?

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:00.030
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
